# Line endings are LF everywhere, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Without this, Git's autocrlf converts text files to CRLF on checkout on
# Windows. That is invisible until something parses a file by anchoring on a
# bare "\n" — and then it does not error, it silently matches nothing. Two real
# failures from exactly that: the design-document renderer reported every
# vendored icon as missing, and five content tests failed on frontmatter that
# was perfectly well-formed.
#
# The nastiest part is that CI never sees it. A Linux runner checks out LF and
# passes, so the breakage only exists on the machine the work is done on.
#
# eol=lf rather than text=auto alone: auto normalises what is committed but
# still hands Windows CRLF in the working tree, which is the half that breaks.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.ico binary
